./core
./error
./number
./stream
./string

+ Size is I64
+ Index is I64
+ Increment is I64

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ Range'Item is Tuple
    is CursorIterable'Item'(Item, Item, Size, Size)
    is Indexable'Item

+ start Item
+ end Item
+ increment Item = Item() + 1
+ is-through = false

╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌ is CursorIterable'Item ╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌

────────────────────
+ get initial-iterator-state (Item, Item, Size, Size) @inline

start, step, 0, length
    .. step = if start <= end then step-size else Item() - step-size

────────────────────
+ do next-iterator ((Item, Item, Size, Size), Item?) @inline
    - state (Item, Item, Size, Size)

if state[3] == 0
    . none Item?
    = (state, none)
if Item.is-integer
    = ((state[0] + state[1], state[1], state[2], state[3] - 1), state[0])
else
    = ((state[0], state[1], state[2] + 1, state[3] - 1), item-at(state[2]))

╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌ is Indexable'Item ╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌

────────────────────
+ get length Size @inline

?! Panic("A range cannot step by 0")
    if increment == Item()
|? Item.is-integer
    |? is-through
        (distance / step + 1) as Size
    |? distance == 0
        0
    ??
        ((distance - 1) / step + 1) as Size
    .. distance = (new-end as I64 as U64) - (new-start as I64 as U64)
    .. step = step-size as U64
??
    whole-steps + final-item-count
    .. whole-steps = (delta / step-size) as Size
    .. final-item-count = if includes-final-item then 1 else 0
    .. includes-final-item = is-through || has-partial-step
    .. has-partial-step = stepped-distance < delta
    .. stepped-distance = (whole-steps as Item) * step-size
    .. delta = new-end - new-start

.. new-start = if start > end then end else start
.. new-end = if start > end then start else end

────────────────────
+ this[index Index] Item @inline

|? index >= 0 && index < length
    item-at(index)
??
    absent(index)

────────────────────
+ this[range Range'Index] Indexable'Item

?! OutOfBoundsError("Range out of bounds ($out-index / $length)")
    if first < 0 || first > length || (count != 0 && last >= length)

|? count == 0
    Range'Item(item-at(first), item-at(first), increment, false)
??
    Range'Item(item-at(first), item-at(last), step-size * (normal.increment as Item), true)

.. normal = range.forward()
.. first = normal.start
.. count = normal.length
.. last = first + (count - 1) * normal.increment
.. out-index = if count == 0 then first else last

╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌

────────────────────
+ this[pos Position]

this[pos.normalize(this)]

╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌ Sequencing and normalization ╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌

────────────────────
+ forward @inline

` The same items from the lowest to the highest, in a range that stops before its end, as
` slices read one.
|? count == 0
    This(start, start, step-size, false)
??
    This(low, high + step-size, step-size, false)

.. count = length
.. far = item-at(count - 1)
.. low = if start > end then far else start
.. high = if start > end then start else far

────────────────────
_ item-at Item @inline
    - index Index

|? start > end
    start - (index as Item) * step-size
??
    start + (index as Item) * step-size

────────────────────
_ do absent Item
    - index Index

?! OutOfBoundsError("Range index $index out of range")

────────────────────
_ get step-size Item @inline

` How far apart the items are: the increment, without its sign, since the range runs from its
` start toward its end whichever way that is.
if increment < Item() then Item() - increment else increment

────────────────────
+ normalize'SeqItem @inline
    - seq Indexable'SeqItem

Range'Index(s, e, i, is-through)

.. len = seq.length
.. s = normalize(start, 0 .. < len)
.. e = normalize(end, 0 .. < len)
.. i = normalize(increment, 0 .. < len)

────────────────────
+ this
    - increment () Item
        - item Item

Stepper(this, increment)

────────────────────
+ to String

"[Range $start $to-or-thru $end by $increment]"
    .. to-or-thru = if is-through then "thru" else "to"

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ Position is Union

| first
| middle
| last
| end
| infinity
| index Index

────────────────────
+ normalize'Item Index @inline
    - seq Indexable'Item

normalize(0 .. < seq.length)

────────────────────
+ normalize'SeqItem Index
    - range Range'SeqItem

match this
    `
    | Position.first
        start
    | Position.middle
        length / 2
    | Position.last
        length - 1
    | Position.end
        length
    | Position.infinity
        Index.max
    | Position.index(n)
        n
    `
    .. start = range.start
    .. length = range.length

╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌ Numeric range types ╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌

╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌ Explicit range constructors ╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ to'RangeItem
    - start RangeItem
    - end RangeItem
    - increment RangeItem?

Range'RangeItem(start, end, increment, false)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ thru'RangeItem
    - start RangeItem
    - end RangeItem
    - increment RangeItem?

Range'RangeItem(start, end, increment, true)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ normalize'T
    - n Int
    - range Range'T

n

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ normalize'T
    - n Position
    - range Range'T

n.normalize(range)
